{"id":"mahabharata-7-067","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":67,"title":"सप्तषष्टितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 67 · Sudakshina and Shrutayudha fall","summary":{"en":"Hemmed in by Drona's forces, Arjuna passes Drona and meets Kritavarman and then the Kamboja king Sudakshina, whom he kills. Shrutayudha, striking Krishna with Varuna's mace, finds it rebound and kill himself, and the army flees.","kn":"ದ್ರೋಣನ ಪಡೆಯಿಂದ ಸುತ್ತುವರಿಯಲ್ಪಟ್ಟ ಅರ್ಜುನ ದ್ರೋಣನನ್ನು ದಾಟಿ ಕೃತವರ್ಮನನ್ನೂ ಕಾಂಬೋಜ ರಾಜ ಸುದಕ್ಷಿಣನನ್ನೂ ಎದುರಿಸಿ ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಶ್ರುತಾಯುಧ ವರುಣನ ಗದೆಯನ್ನು ಕೃಷ್ಣನ ಮೇಲೆ ಎಸೆದಾಗ ಅದು ಮರಳಿ ಅವನನ್ನೇ ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತದೆ; ಸೈನ್ಯ ಓಡುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"द्रोण की सेना से घिरे अर्जुन द्रोण को लाँघकर कृतवर्मा और फिर काम्बोज राजा सुदक्षिण से भिड़ते हैं और उसे मारते हैं। श्रुतायुध वरुण की गदा कृष्ण पर फेंकता है, वह लौटकर उसी को मार देती है और सेना भागती है।","te":"ద్రోణుని బలగాలతో చుట్టుముట్టబడిన అర్జునుడు ద్రోణుని దాటి కృతవర్మను, కాంభోజ రాజు సుదక్షిణుని ఎదుర్కొని చంపుతాడు. శ్రుతాయుధుడు వరుణుని గదను కృష్ణునిపై విసరగా అది తిరిగి అతనినే చంపుతుంది; సేన పారిపోతుంది.","ta":"த்ரோணரின் படையால் சூழப்பட்ட அர்ஜுனன் த்ரோணரைக் கடந்து கிருதவர்மனையும் பின் காம்போஜ மன்னன் சுதக்ஷிணனையும் எதிர்த்துக் கொல்கிறான். ஸ்ருதாயுதன் வருணனின் கதையைக் கண்ணன் மீது எறிய, அது திரும்பி அவனையே கொல்கிறது; படை ஓடுகிறது.","ml":"ദ്രോണരുടെ സേനയാൽ വളയപ്പെട്ട അർജുനൻ ദ്രോണരെ മറികടന്ന് കൃതവർമാവിനെയും പിന്നെ കംബോജരാജാവ് സുദക്ഷിണനെയും കാണുന്നു; അദ്ദേഹത്തെ വധിക്കുന്നു. വരുണന്റെ ഗദയുമായി കൃഷ്ണനെ പ്രഹരിച്ച ശ്രുതായുധൻ, ഗദ തിരിച്ചടിച്ച് സ്വയം മരിക്കുന്നു; സേന ഓടിപ്പോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.67; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"संनिरुद्धस्तु तैः पार्थो महाबलपराक्रमः ।\nद्रुतं समनुयातश्च द्रोणेन रथिनां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha, mighty in strength and valour, was thus hemmed in by them, and Drona, best of charioteers, swiftly came up behind him."}},{"n":2,"text":"किरन्निषुगणांस्तीक्ष्णान्स्वरश्मीनिव भास्करः ।\nतापयामास तत्सैन्यं देहं व्याधिगणो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Scattering showers of sharp arrows as the sun scatters its rays, Arjuna scorched that army as a host of diseases torments the body."}},{"n":3,"text":"अश्वो विद्धो ध्वजश्छिन्नः सारोहः पतितो गजः ।\nछत्राणि चापविद्धानि रथाश्चक्रैर्विना कृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses were pierced, banners cut down, elephants fell with their riders, umbrellas were flung away, and chariots were left without wheels."}},{"n":4,"text":"विद्रुतानि च सैन्यानि शरार्तानि समन्ततः ।\nइत्यासीत्तुमुलं युद्धं न प्राज्ञायत किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Armies fled in all directions, afflicted by arrows; the battle was so confused that nothing could be made out."}},{"n":5,"text":"तेषामायच्छतां संख्ये परस्परमजिह्मगैः ।\nअर्जुनो ध्वजिनीं राजन्नभीक्ष्णं समकम्पयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they strove against one another in the battle with straight-flying arrows, Arjuna, O king, repeatedly made that host tremble."}},{"n":6,"text":"सत्यां चिकीर्षमाणस्तु प्रतिज्ञां सत्यसंगरः ।\nअभ्यद्रवद्रथश्रेष्ठं शोणाश्वं श्वेतवाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wishing to make his vow true, truthful in his resolve, the white-horsed Arjuna rushed at the best of charioteers, the one with the red horses."}},{"n":7,"text":"तं द्रोणः पञ्चविंशत्या मर्मभिद्भिरजिह्मगैः ।\nअन्तेवासिनमाचार्यो महेष्वासं समर्दयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona, his teacher, struck his pupil, the great archer, with twenty-five straight arrows that pierce vital spots."}},{"n":8,"text":"तं तूर्णमिव बीभत्सुः सर्वशस्त्रभृतां वरः ।\nअभ्यधावदिषूनस्यन्निषुवेगविघातकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bibhatsu, best of all weapon-bearers, as though in haste ran at him, shooting arrows that blocked the flight of his arrows."}},{"n":9,"text":"तस्याशु क्षिपतो भल्लान्भल्लैः संनतपर्वभिः ।\nप्रत्यविध्यदमेयात्मा ब्रह्मास्त्रं समुदीरयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Drona swiftly loosed broad arrows, the immeasurable Arjuna answered with smooth-jointed broad arrows, calling up the Brahma weapon."}},{"n":10,"text":"तदद्भुतमपश्याम द्रोणस्याचार्यकं युधि ।\nयतमानो युवा नैनं प्रत्यविध्यद्यदर्जुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We saw that marvel of Drona's teaching in the battle: though the young man tried, Arjuna did not manage to pierce him back."}},{"n":11,"text":"क्षरन्निव महामेघो वारिधाराः सहस्रशः ।\nद्रोणमेघः पार्थशैलं ववर्ष शरवृष्टिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a great cloud pours thousands of streams of water, the cloud Drona rained showers of arrows on the mountain Partha."}},{"n":12,"text":"अर्जुनः शरवर्षं तद्ब्रह्मास्त्रेणैव मारिष ।\nप्रतिजग्राह तेजस्वी बाणैर्बाणान्विशातयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna, radiant, received that rain of arrows with the Brahma weapon itself, O lord, shattering arrows with arrows."}},{"n":13,"text":"द्रोणस्तु पञ्चविंशत्या श्वेतवाहनमार्दयत् ।\nवासुदेवं च सप्तत्या बाह्वोरुरसि चाशुगैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona struck the white-horsed Arjuna with twenty-five arrows, and Vasudeva with seventy swift ones in arms and chest."}},{"n":14,"text":"पार्थस्तु प्रहसन्धीमानाचार्यं स शरौघिणम् ।\nविसृजन्तं शितान्बाणानवारयत तं युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"But wise Partha, laughing, stopped in the battle the teacher, who was loosing floods of sharp arrows."}},{"n":15,"text":"अथ तौ वध्यमानौ तु द्रोणेन रथसत्तमौ ।\nआवर्जयेतां दुर्धर्षं युगान्ताग्निमिवोत्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those two best of chariot-warriors, being struck by Drona, turned aside from him, who was hard to face, like the fire at the end of an age risen up."}},{"n":16,"text":"वर्जयन्निशितान्बाणान्द्रोणचापविनिःसृतान् ।\nकिरीटमाली कौन्तेयो भोजानीकं न्यपातयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Avoiding the sharp arrows from Drona's bow, the garlanded and diademed son of Kunti cut down the army of the Bhojas."}},{"n":17,"text":"सोऽन्तरा कृतवर्माणं काम्बोजं च सुदक्षिणम् ।\nअभ्ययाद्वर्जयन्द्रोणं मैनाकमिव पर्वतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Passing Drona as one passes the mountain Mainaka, he went between Kritavarman and the Kamboja Sudakshina."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततो भोजो नरव्याघ्रं दुःसहः कुरुसत्तम ।\nअविध्यत्तूर्णमव्यग्रो दशभिः कङ्कपत्रिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Bhoja, Kritavarman, hard to bear, best of the Kurus, quickly and calmly struck that tiger among men with ten heron-feathered arrows."}},{"n":19,"text":"तमर्जुनः शितेनाजौ राजन्विव्याध पत्रिणा ।\nपुनश्चान्यैस्त्रिभिर्बाणैर्मोहयन्निव सात्वतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna, O king, pierced him with one sharp arrow, and again with three others, as though bewildering the Satvata."}},{"n":20,"text":"भोजस्तु प्रहसन्पार्थं वासुदेवं च माधवम् ।\nएकैकं पञ्चविंशत्या सायकानां समार्पयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Bhoja, laughing, struck Partha and also Vasudeva, the Madhava, with twenty-five arrows each."}},{"n":21,"text":"तस्यार्जुनो धनुश्छित्त्वा विव्याधैनं त्रिसप्तभिः ।\nशरैरग्निशिखाकारैः क्रुद्धाशीविषसंनिभैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna cut his bow and pierced him with twenty-one arrows that were like tongues of flame and like angry venomous snakes."}},{"n":22,"text":"अथान्यद्धनुरादाय कृतवर्मा महारथः ।\nपञ्चभिः सायकैस्तूर्णं विव्याधोरसि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great chariot-warrior Kritavarman, taking another bow, quickly pierced Arjuna in the chest with five arrows, O Bharata."}},{"n":23,"text":"पुनश्च निशितैर्बाणैः पार्थं विव्याध पञ्चभिः ।\nतं पार्थो नवभिर्बाणैराजघान स्तनान्तरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Again he struck Partha with five sharp arrows, and Partha hit him between the breasts with nine arrows."}},{"n":24,"text":"विषक्तं दृश्य कौन्तेयं कृतवर्मरथं प्रति ।\nचिन्तयामास वार्ष्णेयो न नः कालात्ययो भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Arjuna held fast against Kritavarman's chariot, the Vrishni, Krishna, thought: Let us not lose time."}},{"n":25,"text":"ततः कृष्णोऽब्रवीत्पार्थं कृतवर्मणि मा दयाम् ।\nकुरुसांबन्धिकं कृत्वा प्रमथ्यैनं विशातय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Krishna said to Partha: Show no pity to Kritavarman. Treating him as merely a connection of the Kurus, crush him and strike him down."}},{"n":26,"text":"ततः स कृतवर्माणं मोहयित्वार्जुनः शरैः ।\nअभ्यगाज्जवनैरश्वैः काम्बोजानामनीकिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Arjuna, having stupefied Kritavarman with arrows, went on with his swift horses to the army of the Kambojas."}},{"n":27,"text":"अमर्षितस्तु हार्दिक्यः प्रविष्टे श्वेतवाहने ।\nविधुन्वन्सशरं चापं पाञ्चाल्याभ्यां समागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the white-horsed Arjuna had entered, the son of Hridika, enraged, shaking his bow and arrow, came upon the two Panchalas."}},{"n":28,"text":"चक्ररक्षौ तु पाञ्चाल्यावर्जुनस्य पदानुगौ ।\nपर्यवारयदायान्तौ कृतवर्मा रथेषुभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kritavarman surrounded with chariot-arrows the two Panchalas, guardians of Arjuna's wheels, who followed in his footsteps as they came."}},{"n":29,"text":"तावविध्यत्ततो भोजः सर्वपारशवैः शरैः ।\nत्रिभिरेव युधामन्युं चतुर्भिश्चोत्तमौजसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Bhoja struck them with arrows made wholly of iron, Yudhamanyu with three and Uttamauja with four."}},{"n":30,"text":"तावप्येनं विव्यधतुर्दशभिर्दशभिः शरैः ।\nसंचिच्छिदतुरप्यस्य ध्वजं कार्मुकमेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Each of them pierced him in return with ten arrows, and they also cut down his banner and his bow."}},{"n":31,"text":"अथान्यद्धनुरादाय हार्दिक्यः क्रोधमूर्छितः ।\nकृत्वा विधनुषौ वीरौ शरवर्षैरवाकिरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the son of Hridika, stupefied with rage, took another bow, left the two heroes without bows and buried them under showers of arrows."}},{"n":32,"text":"तावन्ये धनुषी सज्ये कृत्वा भोजं विजघ्नतुः ।\nतेनान्तरेण बीभत्सुर्विवेशामित्रवाहिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two took other bows, strung them, and struck the Bhoja. Meanwhile Bibhatsu entered the enemy host."}},{"n":33,"text":"न लेभाते तु तौ द्वारं वारितौ कृतवर्मणा ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रेष्वनीकेषु यतमानौ नरर्षभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"But those two bulls among men, blocked by Kritavarman, though they strove, found no opening into the Dhritarashtra divisions."}},{"n":34,"text":"अनीकान्यर्दयन्युद्धे त्वरितः श्वेतवाहनः ।\nनावधीत्कृतवर्माणं प्राप्तमप्यरिसूदनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The white-horsed Arjuna, in a hurry, crushing the divisions in battle, did not kill Kritavarman, though that slayer of foes had him within reach."}},{"n":35,"text":"तं दृष्ट्वा तु तथायान्तं शूरो राजा श्रुतायुधः ।\nअभ्यद्रवत्सुसंक्रुद्धो विधुन्वानो महद्धनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him coming so, the brave king Shrutayudha, very angry, rushed at him, shaking his great bow."}},{"n":36,"text":"स पार्थं त्रिभिरानर्छत्सप्तत्या च जनार्दनम् ।\nक्षुरप्रेण सुतीक्ष्णेन पार्थकेतुमताडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He struck Partha with three arrows and Janardana with seventy, and with a very sharp razor-headed arrow hit Partha's banner."}},{"n":37,"text":"तमर्जुनो नवत्या तु शराणां नतपर्वणाम् ।\nआजघान भृशं क्रुद्धस्तोत्त्रैरिव महाद्विपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna, greatly angered, struck him with ninety smooth-jointed arrows, as a great elephant is struck with goads."}},{"n":38,"text":"स तन्न ममृषे राजन्पाण्डवेयस्य विक्रमम् ।\nअथैनं सप्तसप्तत्या नाराचानां समार्पयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He could not bear the Pandava's prowess, O king, and struck Arjuna with seventy-seven iron arrows."}},{"n":39,"text":"तस्यार्जुनो धनुश्छित्त्वा शरावापं निकृत्य च ।\nआजघानोरसि क्रुद्धः सप्तभिर्नतपर्वभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna cut his bow and cut off his quiver, and in anger struck him on the chest with seven smooth-jointed arrows."}},{"n":40,"text":"अथान्यद्धनुरादाय स राजा क्रोधमूर्छितः ।\nवासविं नवभिर्बाणैर्बाह्वोरुरसि चार्पयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the king, stupefied with rage, took another bow and struck Arjuna, the son of Indra, with nine arrows in arms and chest."}},{"n":41,"text":"ततोऽर्जुनः स्मयन्नेव श्रुतायुधमरिंदमः ।\nशरैरनेकसाहस्रैः पीडयामास भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Arjuna, subduer of foes, smiling, tormented Shrutayudha with many thousands of arrows, O Bharata."}},{"n":42,"text":"अश्वांश्चास्यावधीत्तूर्णं सारथिं च महारथः ।\nविव्याध चैनं सप्तत्या नाराचानां महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty chariot-warrior quickly slew his horses and his charioteer, and the very strong Arjuna pierced him with seventy iron arrows."}},{"n":43,"text":"हताश्वं रथमुत्सृज्य स तु राजा श्रुतायुधः ।\nअभ्यद्रवद्रणे पार्थं गदामुद्यम्य वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Leaving his chariot with its slain horses, the valiant king Shrutayudha raised his mace and rushed at Partha in the battle."}},{"n":44,"text":"वरुणस्यात्मजो वीरः स तु राजा श्रुतायुधः ।\nपर्णाशा जननी यस्य शीततोया महानदी ॥","meaning":{"en":"That hero, King Shrutayudha, was a son of Varuna; his mother was the great river Parnasha, cool of water."}},{"n":45,"text":"तस्य माताब्रवीद्वाक्यं वरुणं पुत्रकारणात् ।\nअवध्योऽयं भवेल्लोके शत्रूणां तनयो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"His mother said to Varuna on her son's behalf: Let this son of mine be unslayable by his enemies in the world."}},{"n":46,"text":"वरुणस्त्वब्रवीत्प्रीतो ददाम्यस्मै वरं हितम् ।\nदिव्यमस्त्रं सुतस्तेऽयं येनावध्यो भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Varuna, pleased, said: I give him a boon that will help him: a divine weapon, by which your son will be unslayable."}},{"n":47,"text":"नास्ति चाप्यमरत्वं वै मनुष्यस्य कथंचन ।\nसर्वेणावश्यमर्तव्यं जातेन सरितां वरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"But there is no deathlessness for a man in any way. Everyone born, best of rivers, must surely die."}},{"n":48,"text":"दुर्धर्षस्त्वेष शत्रूणां रणेषु भविता सदा ।\nअस्त्रस्यास्य प्रभावाद्वै व्येतु ते मानसो ज्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet he will always be hard for enemies to overcome in battles; by the power of this weapon let the fever of your mind pass."}},{"n":49,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा वरुणः प्रादाद्गदां मन्त्रपुरस्कृताम् ।\nयामासाद्य दुराधर्षः सर्वलोके श्रुतायुधः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So saying, Varuna gave him a mace consecrated with mantras, by obtaining which Shrutayudha became unassailable in all the world."}},{"n":50,"text":"उवाच चैनं भगवान्पुनरेव जलेश्वरः ।\nअयुध्यति न मोक्तव्या सा त्वय्येव पतेदिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lord of waters, the blessed one, then said to him again: It must not be hurled at one who is not fighting, or it will fall upon you yourself."}},{"n":51,"text":"स तया वीरघातिन्या जनार्दनमताडयत् ।\nप्रतिजग्राह तां कृष्णः पीनेनांसेन वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With that mace, a slayer of heroes, he struck Janardana. Krishna, strong, received it on his broad shoulder."}},{"n":52,"text":"नाकम्पयत शौरिं सा विन्ध्यं गिरिमिवानिलः ।\nप्रत्यभ्ययात्तं विप्रोढा कृत्येव दुरधिष्ठिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"It did not shake Shauri, as wind does not shake the Vindhya mountain; rebounding, like a badly performed sorcery it turned back on him who had sent it."}},{"n":53,"text":"जघान चास्थितं वीरं श्रुतायुधममर्षणम् ।\nहत्वा श्रुतायुधं वीरं जगतीमन्वपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"It killed the valiant, wrathful Shrutayudha as he stood, and having slain the hero Shrutayudha it fell to the earth."}},{"n":54,"text":"हाहाकारो महांस्तत्र सैन्यानां समजायत ।\nस्वेनास्त्रेण हतं दृष्ट्वा श्रुतायुधमरिंदमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great cry of woe arose among the armies, seeing Shrutayudha, subduer of foes, slain by his own weapon."}},{"n":55,"text":"अयुध्यमानाय हि सा केशवाय नराधिप ।\nक्षिप्ता श्रुतायुधेनाथ तस्मात्तमवधीद्गदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"For, O lord of men, Shrutayudha had hurled that mace at Keshava, who was not fighting; therefore the mace killed him."}},{"n":56,"text":"यथोक्तं वरुणेनाजौ तथा स निधनं गतः ।\nव्यसुश्चाप्यपतद्भूमौ प्रेक्षतां सर्वधन्विनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Varuna had said, so he met his end in battle, and fell lifeless to the ground before the eyes of all the bowmen."}},{"n":57,"text":"पतमानस्तु स बभौ पर्णाशायाः प्रियः सुतः ।\nसंभग्न इव वातेन बहुशाखो वनस्पतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he fell, the dear son of Parnasha looked like a many-branched tree broken by the wind."}},{"n":58,"text":"ततः सर्वाणि सैन्यानि सेनामुख्याश्च सर्वशः ।\nप्राद्रवन्त हतं दृष्ट्वा श्रुतायुधमरिंदमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the armies and the leaders of the army everywhere fled, seeing Shrutayudha, subduer of foes, slain."}},{"n":59,"text":"तथ काम्बोजराजस्य पुत्रः शूरः सुदक्षिणः ।\nअभ्ययाज्जवनैरश्वैः फल्गुनं शत्रुसूदनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the brave Sudakshina, son of the Kamboja king, advanced with swift horses against Phalguna, slayer of enemies."}},{"n":60,"text":"तस्य पार्थः शरान्सप्त प्रेषयामास भारत ।\nते तं शूरं विनिर्भिद्य प्राविशन्धरणीतलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha sent seven arrows at him, O Bharata; they pierced that hero and entered the ground."}},{"n":61,"text":"सोऽतिविद्धः शरैस्तीक्ष्णैर्गाण्डीवप्रेषितैर्मृधे ।\nअर्जुनं प्रतिविव्याध दशभिः कङ्कपत्रिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Deeply wounded by sharp arrows loosed from the Gandiva in battle, he pierced Arjuna in return with ten heron-feathered arrows."}},{"n":62,"text":"वासुदेवं त्रिभिर्विद्ध्वा पुनः पार्थं च पञ्चभिः ।\nतस्य पार्थो धनुश्छित्त्वा केतुं चिच्छेद मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having struck Vasudeva with three and Partha again with five, he was met by Partha, who cut his bow and then his banner, O lord."}},{"n":63,"text":"भल्लाभ्यां भृशतीक्ष्णाभ्यां तं च विव्याध पाण्डवः ।\nस तु पार्थं त्रिभिर्विद्ध्वा सिंहनादमथानदत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava pierced him with two very sharp broad arrows. He struck Partha with three and roared a lion-roar."}},{"n":64,"text":"सर्वपारशवीं चैव शक्तिं शूरः सुदक्षिणः ।\nसघण्टां प्राहिणोद्घोरां क्रुद्धो गाण्डीवधन्वने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brave Sudakshina, in anger, hurled at the wielder of the Gandiva a terrible spear with a bell, made wholly of iron."}},{"n":65,"text":"सा ज्वलन्ती महोल्केव तमासाद्य महारथम् ।\nसविस्फुलिङ्गा निर्भिद्य निपपात महीतले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Blazing like a great meteor, it reached that great chariot-warrior with sparks flying, pierced him, and fell to the ground."}},{"n":66,"text":"तं चतुर्दशभिः पार्थो नाराचैः कङ्कपत्रिभिः ।\nसाश्वध्वजधनुःसूतं विव्याधाचिन्त्यविक्रमः ।\nरथं चान्यैः सुबहुभिश्चक्रे विशकलं शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna, of unthinkable valour, pierced him with fourteen heron-feathered iron arrows, his horses, banner, bow and charioteer along with him, and with many others he shattered his chariot to bits."}},{"n":67,"text":"सुदक्षिणं तु काम्बोजं मोघसंकल्पविक्रमम् ।\nबिभेद हृदि बाणेन पृथुधारेण पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava pierced the Kamboja Sudakshina, whose resolve and valour had proved vain, in the heart with a broad-bladed arrow."}},{"n":68,"text":"स भिन्नमर्मा स्रस्ताङ्गः प्रभ्रष्टमुकुटाङ्गदः ।\nपपाताभिमुखः शूरो यन्त्रमुक्त इव ध्वजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His vital parts torn, limbs loosened, crown and armlets fallen away, the hero fell face forward, like a banner-pole released from its fittings."}},{"n":69,"text":"गिरेः शिखरजः श्रीमान्सुशाखः सुप्रतिष्ठितः ।\nनिर्भग्न इव वातेन कर्णिकारो हिमात्यये ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was like a splendid, well-branched, firmly rooted karnikara tree on a mountain peak, broken by the wind at the end of winter."}},{"n":70,"text":"शेते स्म निहतो भूमौ काम्बोजास्तरणोचितः ।\nसुदर्शनीयस्ताम्राक्षः कर्णिना स सुदक्षिणः ।\nपुत्रः काम्बोजराजस्य पार्थेन विनिपातितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Slain, he lay on the ground, worthy of Kamboja coverlets, handsome, red-eyed, Sudakshina, son of the Kamboja king, felled by Partha with the barbed arrow."}},{"n":71,"text":"ततः सर्वाणि सैन्यानि व्यद्रवन्त सुतस्य ते ।\nहतं श्रुतायुधं दृष्ट्वा काम्बोजं च सुदक्षिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all your son's armies fled, seeing Shrutayudha slain and the Kamboja Sudakshina as well."}}]}]}